(Each function passes on the list parameter it was given, so the function
 thirty calls deep grows the caller's own list.)
To 'fill' with a list called items.
    For each number from 1 to 40, append the number to items.

To 'go down' with a list called items and a number called depth.
    If depth is 30, 'fill' of items.
    If depth is less than 30, 'go down' of items and depth add 1.

a list called xs is [0].
'go down' of xs and 1.
Print "length: {xs's length}, last: {xs's last}".
